* Behavioural NE555 timer (bipolar) for the Monaco GP sound references.
* Typical data-sheet behaviour, not a measured part: the internal 5K/5K/5K
* divider from vcc sets CONTROL (2/3 vcc) and the trigger level (half of
* CONTROL); the threshold comparator resets and the trigger comparator sets
* the latch; RESET below 0.7 V resets it and dominates. OUTPUT is vcc - 1.7 V
* high (3.3 V at 5 V, TI SLFS022 typical) and 0.05 V low; DISCHARGE sinks
* through 10 ohm while the output is low. Uses ngspice's XSPICE digital
* models.
* Pins: gnd tr out res ctl th dis vcc (1..8)
.subckt NE555 gnd tr out res ctl th dis vcc
R1 vcc ctl 5k
R2 ctl tl 5k
R3 tl gnd 5k
Bthr thr_d gnd V=V(th)-V(ctl)
Btrg trg_d gnd V=V(tl)-V(tr)
Bres res_d gnd V=0.7-V(res)
Bone one_a gnd V=1
Aadc [thr_d trg_d res_d one_a] [thr trg rst one] adc555
.model adc555 adc_bridge(in_low=-1e-12 in_high=1e-12)
Aor [thr rst] rr or555
.model or555 d_or(rise_delay=1e-9 fall_delay=1e-9)
* trigger only while not in reset
Arn rst rstn inv555
.model inv555 d_inverter(rise_delay=1e-9 fall_delay=1e-9)
Aand [trg rstn] ss and555
.model and555 d_and(rise_delay=1e-9 fall_delay=1e-9)
Alat ss rr one NULL NULL q qb lat555
.model lat555 d_srlatch(sr_delay=1e-9 enable_delay=1e-9 set_delay=1e-9 reset_delay=1e-9 ic=0 sr_value=1 rise_delay=1e-9 fall_delay=1e-9)
Adac [q qb] [qo qbo] dac555
.model dac555 dac_bridge(out_low=0 out_high=1 t_rise=1e-8 t_fall=1e-8)
Bout out gnd V=0.05+(V(vcc,gnd)-1.75)*V(qo)
Sdis dis gnd qbo gnd swdis
.model swdis SW(VT=0.5 VH=0.05 RON=10 ROFF=1e10)
.ends NE555
